  "sn55.7:3.1": "“Relevant for oneself” is <i lang='pi' translate='no'>attupanāyika</i>, where <i lang='pi' translate='no'>upanāyika</i> is a form of <i lang='pi' translate='no'>opaneyyika</i>, a standard epithet of the Dhamma. The root sense is “leading near”, but here we see that the applied sense is “applicable to oneself”, i.e. “relevant”. See also <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thag1.1/en/sujato#1.4'>Thag 1.1:1.4</a>. ",
